[2026-03-14T21:40:22.273Z] {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_018nzjRYzXVzBH22JFzioQ1V","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Vite correctly serves `text/javascript`. The problem is that netlify dev's proxy is applying the `/* → /index.html` redirect BEFORE forwarding to Vite. This is a netlify dev bug/misconfiguration.\n\nThe issue is in the redirect order in `netlify.toml`. The `/*` catch-all redirect matches everything, including module requests. In production, Vite builds everything into `/assets/` which wouldn't match `/api/*`. But in dev mode, the source files like `/src/main.tsx` match `/*` and get redirected to `/index.html`.\n\nThe fix: the `/*` redirect should only apply to HTML navigation requests, not to module/asset requests. But netlify.toml doesn't have MIME-type based conditions. The real fix is to change the redirect to be more specific, or to ensure the netlify dev proxy forwards to Vite before applying redirects.\n\nActually, looking at this more carefully - netlify dev should proxy all requests to Vite first and only apply redirects for 404s. Let me check if there's a setting for this.\n\nActually, the issue might be simpler. The `base` setting in `netlify.toml` is `apps/GoogleFlights` which affects how the dev server resolves paths. Let me check what netlify dev's resolved config looks like:\n\nLooking at the test run 7 log earlier:\n```\nbuild:\n    base: /repo/apps/GoogleFlights\n```\n\nThis is correct. The issue is really that the SPA redirect catches all requests. In newer versions of netlify, you can use `force = false` on redirects (which is the default), meaning the redirect only applies if the URL doesn't match a real file. But in dev mode, the \"real files\" are served by Vite, not from the filesystem.\n\nLet me try a different approach - remove the catch-all redirect from the config since Vite's dev server handles SPA routing:\n\nActually, a simpler fix: let me check if adding `force = false` to the catch-all redirect helps, or better yet, use netlify dev's built-in framework detection without the SPA redirect:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":357,"cache_read_input_tokens":106078,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":357,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ac218b6b-bf51-424d-b90a-443e75c6a1b6","uuid":"d7effc24-bbc0-4d05-9147-990d5ac0fa66"}
