[2026-03-14T22:12:26.839Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user assigned a task to fix tests in `tests/airport-autocomplete.spec.ts` for the GoogleFlights app, following the skill file at `skills/tasks/build/testing.md`. The task was part of a worker queue system. The subtask was \"FixTests: tests/airport-autocomplete.spec.ts\". After completing all subtasks, I should output `<DONE>`.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Playwright testing with custom browser configuration\n   - Netlify Functions v2 (Request/Response API) execution in worker_threads\n   - Vite dev server with proxy configuration\n   - Neon serverless PostgreSQL database connections\n   - ARM64 vs x86-64 binary compatibility (OrbStack environment)\n   - Netlify CLI internal flags (`--internal-disable-edge-functions`, `--offline`)\n   - Ephemeral Neon database branches for test isolation\n   - Custom Node.js HTTP server for Netlify Functions\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/scripts/test.ts`\n     - The main test orchestration script. Manages Neon branch creation, schema init, seeding, server startup, Playwright execution, and cleanup.\n     - Major changes: Replaced netlify dev server startup with custom functions server + Vite approach. Added process cleanup for `functions-server`. Added 1s wait after killing stale processes.\n     - Key section (server startup):\n     ```typescript\n     // Step 5a: Start custom functions server\n     log('Starting functions server...')\n     const functionsProc = spawn('npx', ['tsx', 'scripts/functions-server.ts', '9999'], {\n       cwd: appDir,\n       env: { ...process.env, DATABASE_URL: testDbUrl },\n       stdio: ['ignore', 'pipe', 'pipe'],\n     })\n     // ... wait for functions server ready ...\n     \n     // Step 5b: Start vite dev server (proxies /api to functions server on 9999)\n     log('Starting vite dev server...')\n     const serverProc = spawn('npx', ['vite', '--host', '127.0.0.1', '--port', '8888', '--strictPort'], {\n       cwd: appDir,\n       env: { ...process.env, DATABASE_URL: testDbUrl },\n       stdio: ['ignore', 'pipe', 'pipe'],\n     })\n     ```\n     - Process cleanup section:\n     ```typescript\n     try { execSync('pkill -f \"netlify dev\" 2>/dev/null || true', { stdio: 'ignore' }) } catch { /* ignore */ }\n     try { execSync('pkill -f \"functions-server\" 2>/dev/null || true', { stdio: 'ignore' }) } catch { /* ignore */ }\n     try { execSync('pkill -f \"node.*vite\" 2>/dev/null || true', { stdio: 'ignore' }) } catch { /* ignore */ }\n     await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 1000))\n     ```\n\n   - `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/scripts/functions-server.ts` (NEW FILE)\n     - Custom lightweight HTTP server that directly loads and executes Netlify Functions without worker_threads isolation, avoiding the ECONNREFUSED issue.\n     - Full content:\n     ```typescript\n     import { createServer } from 'http'\n     import { join, basename } from 'path'\n     import { readdirSync } from 'fs'\n\n     const functionsDir = join(import.meta.dirname, '..', 'netlify', 'functions')\n     const port = parseInt(process.argv[2] || '9999')\n\n     const functionModules: Record<string, { default: (req: Request, ctx: unknown) => Promise<Response> }> = {}\n\n     const files = readdirSync(functionsDir).filter(f => f.endsWith('.ts') && f !== 'db.ts')\n     for (const file of files) {\n       const name = basename(file, '.ts')\n       functionModules[name] = await import(join(functionsDir, file))\n     }\n\n     console.log(`Loaded ${Object.keys(functionModules).length} functions: ${Object.keys(functionModules).join(', ')}`)\n\n     const server = createServer(async (req, res) => {\n       const url = new URL(req.url || '/', `http://localhost:${port}`)\n       let funcName: string | null = null\n       const apiMatch = url.pathname.match(/^\\/api\\/([^/]+)/)\n       const netlifyMatch = url.pathname.match(/^\\/.netlify\\/functions\\/([^/]+)/)\n\n       if (apiMatch?.[1]) {\n         funcName = apiMatch[1]\n       } else if (netlifyMatch?.[1]) {\n         funcName = netlifyMatch[1]\n       }\n\n       if (!funcName || !functionModules[funcName]) {\n         res.writeHead(404)\n         res.end('Not found')\n         return\n       }\n\n       try {\n         const headers = new Headers()\n         for (const [key, value] of Object.entries(req.headers)) {\n           if (value) headers.set(key, Array.isArray(value) ? value[0]! : value)\n         }\n\n         const requestUrl = `http://localhost:${port}${req.url}`\n         const requestInit: RequestInit = { method: req.method, headers }\n\n         if (req.method !== 'GET' && req.method !== 'HEAD') {\n           const chunks: Buffer[] = []\n           for await (const chunk of req) { chunks.push(chunk as Buffer) }\n           requestInit.body = Buffer.concat(chunks)\n         }\n\n         const request = new Request(requestUrl, requestInit)\n         const response = await functionModules[funcName]!.default(request, {})\n\n         res.writeHead(response.status, {\n           'Content-Type': response.headers.get('content-type') || 'application/json',\n           'Access-Control-Allow-Origin': '*',\n         })\n         const body = await response.text()\n         res.end(body)\n       } catch (err: unknown) {\n         const error = err as Error\n         console.error(`Function ${funcName} error:`, error.message)\n         res.writeHead(500)\n         res.end(JSON.stringify({ error: error.message }))\n       }\n     })\n\n     server.listen(port, () => {\n       console.log(`Functions server ready on port ${port}`)\n     })\n     ```\n\n   - `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/vite.config.ts`\n     - Added proxy configuration for API routes to functions server\n     ```typescript\n     server: {\n       proxy: {\n         '/api': {\n           target: 'http://localhost:9999',\n           changeOrigin: true,\n         },\n       },\n     },\n     ```\n\n   - `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/playwright.config.ts`\n     - Removed Replay browser (`getExecutablePath`) since it's x86-64 only\n     - Changed to use default Playwright Chromium (ARM64 compatible)\n     - Updated webServer and baseURL\n     ```typescript\n     import { defineConfig, devices } from '@playwright/test'\n\n     export default defineConfig({\n       testDir: './tests',\n       testIgnore: ['**/deployment.spec.ts'],\n       timeout: 60000,\n       expect: { timeout: 10000 },\n       fullyParallel: false,\n       retries: 0,\n       workers: 1,\n       reporter: [['list'], ['json', { outputFile: 'test-results/results.json' }]],\n       use: {\n         baseURL: 'http://localhost:8888',\n         trace: 'on-first-retry',\n       },\n       projects: [\n         {\n           name: 'replay-chromium',\n           use: { ...devices['Desktop Chrome'] },\n         },\n       ],\n       webServer: {\n         command: 'npx vite --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8888 --strictPort',\n         port: 8888,\n         reuseExistingServer: true,\n         timeout: 30000,\n       },\n     })\n     ```\n\n   - `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/package.json`\n     - Updated dev command: `\"dev\": \"vite --host 127.0.0.1 --port 5173 --strictPort\"`\n\n   - `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/tests/airport-autocomplete.spec.ts` - NOT modified, all 11 tests pass as-is\n   - `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/src/components/AirportAutocomplete.tsx` - Read for understanding, NOT modified\n   - `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/src/pages/SearchPage.tsx` - Read for understanding, NOT modified\n   - `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/netlify/functions/airports.ts` - Read for understanding, NOT modified\n   - `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/netlify/functions/db.ts` - Read for understanding, NOT modified\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **Server start timeout (no --offline)**: `netlify dev` required `--offline` flag in container. Fixed by adding `--offline`.\n   - **Port 5173 conflict**: Stale vite processes held port 5173, causing vite to start on 5174 while netlify dev waited for 5173. Fixed with `--strictPort` and explicit `--host 127.0.0.1` in dev command.\n   - **Deno/Edge Functions crash**: Netlify CLI tried to set up Deno for Edge Functions. Deno binary was x86 on ARM64. Fixed with `--internal-disable-edge-functions` flag discovered by reading netlify CLI source at `/usr/local/lib/node_modules/netlify-cli/dist/utils/proxy.js` line 687.\n   - **Replay browser x86-64 on ARM64**: `/home/agent/.replay/runtimes/chrome-linux/chrome` is x86-64 ELF binary. All tests failed with \"OrbStack ERROR: Dynamic loader not found: /lib64/ld-linux-x86-64.so.2\". Fixed by removing `getExecutablePath('chromium')` from playwright config and using default Playwright Chromium at `/home/agent/.pw-browsers/chromium-1208/` (ARM64).\n   - **MIME type error - SPA redirect catching module scripts**: `/* → /index.html` redirect in `netlify.toml` caught Vite module script requests, returning `text/html` instead of `text/javascript`. React app didn't render. Fixed by having tests use Vite directly instead of netlify dev proxy.\n   - **Netlify dev function execution ECONNREFUSED**: Functions v2 run in `worker_threads` via `lambda-local`. Neon serverless HTTP connections failed with `ECONNREFUSED 127.0.0.1:XXXXX` on random ports. Root cause: worker thread isolation issue in netlify CLI. Fixed by creating custom `functions-server.ts` that runs functions directly in the main process.\n   - **Port 9999 EADDRINUSE**: Previous test run's functions server still held port 9999. Fixed by adding `pkill -f \"functions-server\"` to cleanup step and 1s wait.\n   - **TypeScript errors in functions-server.ts**: `undefined` not assignable to `string | null`, array access possibly undefined. Fixed with optional chaining (`apiMatch?.[1]`), non-null assertions 